Code that shows `\end{minted}` — on a line of its own, indented, or after
other text — printed only up to it in LaTeX, and stopped the build.

```latex
\begin{minted}{js}
const greet = (name) => `Hello, ${name}!`;
\end{minted}
```

The same language again:

```latex
\begin{listing}[htbp]
\begin{minted}{python}
print("hello, world")
  \end{minted}
\caption{A hello-world program}
\end{listing}
```

No language, and the end after other text:

```
see \end{minted} here
```

One that shows its own environment's end as well:

```latex
\end{minted}
\end{jmdmintedlatex}
```

An ordinary block is as it was:

```python
print("unchanged")
```

The paragraph after them prints.
